From: egui-aros
Subject: [PATCH] egui-winit: use the AROS clipboard instead of arboard

Crate: egui-winit 0.37.0 from storytold/egui 6d518fc799681571963842f95b55a6b68431b15a,
  manifest made standalone by scripts/ea.py.
Date: 2026-10-28 (rebased from the egui-winit 0.36.2 series of 2026-10-19)
Problem: the `clipboard` feature, which eframe always enables, builds
  arboard on every target but Android. On AROS arboard takes its X11 path
  (x11rb, rustix), which does not compile for x86_64-aros, and there is no
  X server to talk to.
Rationale: aros-gui-sys (AROS tools/crosstools/rust/crates) already has the
  system clipboard: unit 0 as IFF FTXT through iffparse.library. Text is
  converted to and from ISO-8859-1, the encoding that glue documents.
  Without a system clipboard text the in-process fallback is kept.
Scope: arboard is not built on AROS; get/set_text try the AROS clipboard
  first. Images are not copied (as before, an error is logged).
Upstream-status: candidate for the AROS contrib crate store (not submitted).
Prerequisites: aros-gui-sys (AROS bf7075aa).
Limitations: characters outside ISO-8859-1 are written as `?`; FTXT read
  from programs that store another 8-bit charset is read as ISO-8859-1.
Verification: see the egui-aros build records (branch egui-0.37).
Rebase: the 0.37 clipboard also has winit's Wayland clipboard and the
  PRIMARY selection (both Linux-only); every arboard gate that excluded
  Android and iOS now excludes AROS too.
Removal: when the AROS crate store carries an equivalent change.
